// Yoopanese (U.P. Michigan) translation of Snow War tiers 1–144 (No Ammo through Spreader Rail Head).
// Keys are the exact English labels from SNOW_WAR_TIERS in index.html.
window.YOOPER = window.YOOPER || {};
window.YOOPER.SNOW_WAR_TIERS = Object.assign(window.YOOPER.SNOW_WAR_TIERS || {}, {
  "No Ammo": { label: "No Ammo, Eh", desc: "Not one packable flake across da whole measured area. Da snow war only exists in stories from older brothers an' sisters, an' every one of 'em puts it in a different year and nobody agrees on how many guys were in it. Zero throws tried, zero landed, an' da season opens wit' da ledger blank." },
  "Sketch on Graph Paper": { label: "Sketch on Da Graph Paper", desc: "Dere's no snow anywhere in da measured area, so da war gets fought on paper instead, ya know. A fella draws a machine at four squares to da inch: a screw inside a trough, two wheels, a handle, an' an arrow labelled “snow goes here.” Nuttin' on it has a dimension, an' one wheel's drawn larger dan da other. It's da first entry in a design record dat's gonna run, by da local count, some forty thousand years." },
  "Molecular": { label: "Molecular, Eh", desc: "Dere's frozen water at da molecular level an' nowhere else. Maybe one hundred-thousandth of an inch on any given surface, which is about a thousand molecules deep, yah. No instrument on da block can pick it up, an' no way ya pile it makes a projectile." },
  "Dimensioned Drawing": { label: "Drawin' Wit' Numbers", desc: "Da sketch gets numbers: an eleven-centimetre screw in a half-round trough, a seven-centimetre pitch, an' a flight depth of three and three quarter centimetres, picked so an acorn clears wit' room. Measured snow depth is five hundred-thousandths of an inch, which is to say none, eh. Da drawing gets checked twice an' comes out consistent, which is more dan ya can say for da weather." },
  "Subatomic": { label: "Subatomic", desc: "Dere's frozen stuff technically dere at one ten-thousandth of an inch. Ya need instruments to confirm it, an' closin' a fist around da whole supply changes nuttin' — not da mass, not da shape, not da temperature. Block-wide yield works out to a thousandth of one snowball." },
  "Screw Pitch Argument": { label: "Arguin' Over Da Screw Pitch", desc: "Two guys spend a whole afternoon on whedder da screw oughta turn six times per wheel revolution or eight. Six wins, since walkin' pace already moves a litre an' a half a second an' nobody can walk faster to prove otherwise. Da whole ting gets settled wit'out any material: da ground's got two ten-thousandths of an inch on it, an' neither guy goes outside to check." },
  "Instrument-Only": { label: "Only Da Gauge Knows", desc: "Depth hits four ten-thousandths of an inch — enough for a sensitive gauge to read, not enough for a hand to feel, ya know. Two separate readings agree to within ten percent, an' dat's da best evidence of snow anybody's gonna get dis week. Nuttin' to lift, pack, or throw." },
  "Cardboard Mock-Up": { label: "Cardboard Mock-Up, Eh", desc: "A full-size shell gets cut outta a shipping box an' taped togedder to prove it fits in a school backpack. It does, at thirty by forty-two by fifteen centimetres, fillin' most of a nineteen-litre pack, which was da whole point. It can't spread nuttin', holds no load, an' falls apart when ya set it down on wet ground — of which dere's seven ten-thousandths of an inch." },
  "Theoretical": { label: "Just in Theory", desc: "Da snowball exists as a math ting wit' a set radius, density, an' trajectory. Ya can describe it, draw it, an' spec it out to four decimal places, but at a thousandth of an inch of coverage ya can't build it, eh. Every engagement anybody plans comes out to zero throws a side." },
  "Gear Train Laid Out": { label: "Gear Train All Laid Out", desc: "Da drive gets worked out end to end: a ring gear inside each wheel hub, a pinion on da screw shaft, six to one, an' a detent clutch between 'em set to let go below anyting dat could hurt a hand. Every number in it's borrowed outta a catalogue an' none of 'em's been tested. Material on hand is sixteen ten-thousandths of an inch, so da clutch got nuttin' to protect anybody from yet." },
  "Anecdotal": { label: "A Guy Says", desc: "Somebody tells about packin' one. Da story's real detailed — three inches across, thrown forty feet, a confirmed hit — an' ya can't check a bit of it. Four witnesses were supposedly dere, an' two of 'em won't back it up. Measured depth: two and a half thousandths of an inch, eh." },
  "First Printed Screw": { label: "First Printed Screw", desc: "Nine hours on a borrowed printer makes a screw in two half-shells, split down da axis since a helix won't pull outta a two-part mould. Da halves get glued, da seam sticks up half a millimetre da whole length, an' da shaft bore comes out oval. It turns in yer hand. Dere's nuttin' to put in it, though: measured depth is three and a half thousandths of an inch." },
  "Rumored": { label: "Heard It Down at Da Bar", desc: "Somebody says dey packed one just fine. Nobody can do it again in maybe forty tries after, dere's no photograph, an' no physical evidence lasts more dan about ninety seconds in open air, ya know. Da claim gets written down, argued over, an' left hangin' for da season." },
  "Trough Fit Check": { label: "Checkin' Da Trough Fit", desc: "Da screw gets dropped in its half-round trough an' da clearance gets measured at eight points. Target was three millimetres; readings run two to five and a half, wit' dat proud seam catchin' at one o’clock every rotation. A guy files it back by hand over about forty minutes. Still no snow, an' da check goes down as passed." },
  "Disputed": { label: "Dat's Not How It Went", desc: "Two stories about da same throw disagree on every point ya could measure: da range, da size, whedder it even landed. Depth is a hundredth of an inch, which'll mark up a dark sleeve but won't make a projectile, eh. Da block splits about even an' neither side can show ya a sample." },
  "Clutch Bench Test": { label: "Clutch on Da Bench", desc: "Da slip clutch gets loaded up on a kitchen scale an' a lever arm till it lets go, thirty-one times in a row, at a torque dat varies under eight percent between tries. It's da first number in da whole project dat got measured instead of picked, ya know. Snow on da ground: fourteen thousandths of an inch, none of it able to jam nuttin'." },
  "Imperceptible": { label: "Can't Hardly Tell", desc: "Enough to whiten a dark pair of choppers for about two seconds before it goes right back to air. Two hundredths of an inch on every exposed surface, an' any try at packin' it sends it right back up where it came from. Block-wide yield is one marginal snowball, an' it don't hold." },
  "Dry Run, No Load": { label: "Dry Run, Nuttin' In It", desc: "Da whole machine gets pushed down a hallway wit' an empty trough to make sure da wheels drive da screw an' da screw quits da second ya quit pushin'. Both hold, over eleven passes. Only ting it puts out is a little clickin' from da pinion, an' da operator gets told twice to take it outside, eh." },
  "Barely There": { label: "Just a Skiff", desc: "Ya can see it across da whole lawn at a glance an' ya can't see it at arm’s length. Three hundredths of an inch is enough to outline a footprint for about a minute before it fills back in. Sweep four hundred square feet an' ya get a marble-sized lump dat lasts maybe a second in a closed hand." },
  "Flour Trial": { label: "Da Flour Test", desc: "Testin' starts indoors wit' da only pourable white stuff in da house. Two kilograms of flour lay a band twenty-eight centimetres wide an' about four millimetres deep across nine feet of kitchen floor, coefficient of variation under twenty percent by cell count. Machine's proven. Da kitchen don't recover for two days, an' nobody does dat again, believe you me." },
  "A Pinch": { label: "Just a Pinch", desc: "Strip a whole porch railing — twelve linear feet — an' ya get someting about pea-sized, maybe half an inch across. It falls apart inside four feet of flight an' leaves no mark where it hits. Two guys, six minutes strippin' for one throw each, an' da supply's gone inside a minute, eh." },
  "Birdseed Calibration": { label: "Birdseed Calibration", desc: "Birdseed takes over for flour since at least ya can sweep it up. Runs at each gate detent — closed, four millimetres, twelve, thirty-five — give a nice clean flow curve of eleven, ninety, an' three hundred and forty grams per metre. Da gate's confirmed to meter, not just open. Snow outside dat week totals six hundredths of an inch an' ain't part of it." },
  "Thimbleful": { label: "A Thimbleful, Eh", desc: "Seven hundredths of an inch, which is a thimble’s worth off ten square feet of clean surface. A packed one gets to three quarters of an inch an' holds togedder for about six feet of flight. Ya can have three or four at once if ya strip every car, railing, an' step on da property — about forty surfaces over twenty minutes." },
  "Sand Run": { label: "Sand Run", desc: "A bag of play sand tests da machine against someting wit' real heft: eleven kilograms through da trough in one afternoon wit'out a jam, dough da wheels slip on smooth concrete about one push in six. Slip gets written down as da design’s weakest spot an' don't get fixed. Everybody agrees sand acts nuttin' like snow, which nobody dere has spread yet, ya know." },
  "Scrapings": { label: "Scrapin's", desc: "Scrape da whole hood of a car, about fifteen square feet, an' ya get one crumbly lump wit' no core to it. It makes it maybe two feet before it goes back to loose crystals. A couple stubborn guys workin' da whole block, thirty-one car hoods over twenty-five minutes, can make five or six, an' none of 'em land in one piece." },
  "Acorn-Loaded": { label: "Loaded Up Wit' Acorns", desc: "A fella shows up wit' a backpack spreader an' no snow to put in it, so da hopper gets filled wit' acorns off da ground — same test stuff da machine got proven on back in September. Gate goes to its widest detent an' eleven acorns get laid in a perfect even line across four feet of bare pavement. Everybody dere agrees dis ain't ammunition. It goes in da record anyhow, 'cause da machine worked perfect an' somebody oughta say so." },
  "Gate Detents Set": { label: "Gate Detents Set", desc: "After da acorn run da gate gets four hard stops instead of a friction slide: closed, four millimetres for a dustin', twelve for snow, thirty-five for acorns an' mulch. Each detent gets checked by pushin' three metres over a tarp an' weighin' what lands. Repeatability over ten runs holds within nine percent, which is better dan da snowfall it was built for ever managed, eh." },
  "Sweepings": { label: "Sweepin's", desc: "An eighth of an inch, gathered up by sweepin' instead of scoopin'. Ya get about one round per thirty square feet, at an inch and a quarter across an' mostly grit. Ten to twelve can get put togedder in twenty minutes, an' about two in three fall apart when ya let go." },
  "Wheel Slip Failure": { label: "Wheels Spinnin'", desc: "Da first honest failure. On packed snow at a tenth of an inch da tread glazes up an' da wheels turn wit'out drivin' da screw, output droppin' to a third of da bench number over da same distance. Nuttin' breaks, which is da design doin' what it's supposed to — a slippin' wheel spreads thin instead of snappin' a shaft. Da whole ting gets written up, includin' da part where it didn't work, ya know." },
  "A Dusting’s Worth": { label: "A Dustin's Worth", desc: "Dere's snow on da ground ya can see, an' ya can see dere ain't enough of it. Coverage is unbroken over every surface, an' a packed round gets to an inch and a half before it starts sheddin'. Keepin' up fire is impossible: da whole yard's good for about two throws each for four guys." },
  "Lug Tread Retrofit": { label: "Lug Tread Retrofit", desc: "Deep paddle lugs get cut into da tread bands wit' a jackknife, eight per wheel, on da idea dat a wheel dat can't glaze can't slip. Drive comes back to about eighty percent of bench output on da same packed surface. Now da wheels leave a track dat four different people figure is from some little critter, eh." },
  "Half a Snowball": { label: "Half a Snowball", desc: "Just short of enough for one whole round. What ya can pack gets to an inch and three quarters, holds its shape in yer hand, an' splits at da seam when ya let go about half da time. Da whole yard's good for one usable throw an' one dat's gonna get argued about." },
  "First Snow Contact": { label: "First Real Snow, Eh", desc: "Da machine meets real snow for da first time, nineteen hundredths of an inch of it, scraped off two car roofs an' poured into da buffer by hand. It lays a band eleven feet long before it runs dry. Da layer's even, it's snow on bare pavement for sure, an' it lasts four minutes. Pictures get taken from down low so ya can't see da bare ground past da band." },
  "One Bad Snowball": { label: "One Crummy Snowball", desc: "One snowball, maybe two inches across, packed real bad — mostly grass an' driveway grit, eh. Somebody chucks it once from maybe twenty feet, it misses, an' dere's nuttin' left to make a second one. Da whole ting's over in under ten seconds, one guy on each side." },
  "Jammed Spreader": { label: "Spreader's Jammed Up", desc: "Da block’s one spreader sucks a pebble into da screw an' da slip clutch does just what it was built for: da wheels keep turnin', nuttin' snaps, an' no snow comes out da back. Clearin' it takes forty seconds wit' a gloved hand an' da finger grille lifted. Durin' dem forty seconds da operator's a sittin' duck, gets hit twice, an' files da season’s first formal complaint about equipment reliability." },
  "Clutch Slips As Designed": { label: "Clutch Slips Like It Oughta", desc: "Anudder jam, dis time a frozen stick, an' da clutch lets go before da operator notices anyting but a change in da sound. Whole interruption is nine seconds. Da bench number from da kitchen scale holds in da cold to within eleven percent, which retires da last untested number in da machine. It's da only piece of equipment on da block dat's never broke, ya know." },
  "One Good Snowball": { label: "One Good Snowball", desc: "Enough clean stuff for one real packed round: two and a quarter inches, even all da way through, no junk in it. It carries thirty-five feet an' shows up in one piece. Dere's exactly one on da property, both sides know where it's at, it changes hands twice before anybody throws it, an' da engagement is a single throw, eh." },
  "Five-Millimetre Layer": { label: "Five-Millimetre Layer", desc: "Da spec gets met outdoors for da first time: a five-millimetre layer across a twenty-eight-centimetre swath at walkin' pace, gridded into ten cells an' counted, coefficient of variation seventeen percent. From four feet away da driveway looks freshly snowed on. From right above it looks like a stripe, an' da operator spends da next twenty minutes walkin' parallel passes to fix dat." },
  "Two Snowballs": { label: "Two Snowballs, Eh", desc: "Enough for exactly one throw each at two and a half inches across. Both get let go in da same second from thirty feet, one connects, an' da yard — about forty feet by sixty — is stripped bare after. Da whole engagement runs four seconds, an' total supply at da first throw is two." },
  "Wings Deployed": { label: "Wings Out", desc: "Da fold-out wings get used for real da first time, ridin' da verge where a shovelled bank meets bare concrete an' funnellin' a forty-eight-centimetre intake into da twenty-eight-centimetre mouth. Run length quits bein' limited by da buffer an' starts bein' limited by da snowbank, which is da whole point of da design, ya know. One pass covers sixty feet wit'out a reload." },
  "Handful": { label: "A Handful, Yah", desc: "A stockpile of six to eight fits inside one chopper. Ammo gets rationed right off da bat at two throws a minute an' it's all gone within ninety seconds of da first exchange. Two to four guys, no fixed positions, an' no resupply anywhere on da property, eh." },
  "Surge Buffer Proof": { label: "Provin' Da Surge Buffer", desc: "Da wings get fed in stop-an'-go bursts on purpose to see if da five-litre buffer smooths out da surges or just stores 'em up. Coefficient of variation wit' da buffer full runs fourteen percent against twenty-nine empty, over three matched runs. One part's doin' two jobs — surge damper on da verge, hopper on bare ground — an' it's da last piece of da design nobody'd proven yet, ya know." },
  "Mitten Sling": { label: "Chopper Sling", desc: "Da first try at a gadget: a round dropped in a loose mitten, swung twice overhead, an' let go by feel alone. It carries forty-five feet against a hand throw’s twenty-five, an' about one in nine lands within ten feet of whatever ya aimed at. Two mittens end up on da roof in da first hour, eh." },
  "Hand-Crank Prototype": { label: "Hand-Crank Prototype", desc: "An older brother drags out dat rejected crank-auger design, da one where da operator's gotta turn a handle an' steer at da same time. It throws snow in a pretty decent arc for about thirty seconds, an' den da guy's arm gives out. Dere's two on da block an' neither one makes it through da afternoon in one piece. Da backpack roller's agreed, once again an' for da record, to be da right design, ya know." },
  "The Crank Is Abandoned": { label: "Da Crank Gets Tossed", desc: "Both crank augers get stripped for parts within an hour of failin', an' da decision goes in da record wit' a reason instead of a verdict: a machine dat wants a turnin' arm an' a steerin' arm at once has one arm too few. Da wheel drive stands unchallenged from here on out. Da cranks’ handles get kept an' used, over da next few weeks, for stuff dat's got nuttin' to do wit' it." },
  "Pocketful": { label: "A Pocketful", desc: "Ten to twelve rounds, carried in coat pockets 'cause dere's noplace else to put 'em. Effective range gets to twenty-five feet an' hit rate runs about one in five. Both sides start at full supply an' da whole ting's decided within two minutes by whoever throws slower, eh." },
  "Continuous Side-Feed": { label: "Side-Feed All Day Long", desc: "Da main mode goes live: walk da boundary, wings in da bank, an' lay cover forever wit'out ever openin' da lid. Two hundred and forty feet of stripped ground gets resurfaced in one straight push of about six minutes. Ammo supply quits dependin' on where da snow fell an' starts dependin' on who's willin' to walk, ya know." },
  "Skirmish": { label: "Little Skirmish", desc: "Real snowballs, for a bit — about a dozen a side at three inches across. Both sides run dry inside two minutes, before anybody finds cover, an' it ends 'cause da supply's gone, not 'cause anybody decided anyting. Hit rate holds around one in four at da usual twenty-five-foot range, eh." },
  "Lacrosse Scoop": { label: "Lacrosse Scoop", desc: "Turns out a plastic sand scoop holds a round an' throws it wit'out packin' it any more. Range runs fifty feet, da round comes off in one piece nine times in ten, an' one guy can load an' throw wit'out settin' nuttin' down. It becomes da standard tool for anybody who can't throw hard." },
  "Second Unit Built": { label: "Built Anudder One", desc: "A second machine gets printed from da same files over two nights, wit' da seam problem fixed in da model instead of filed out by hand. Da two are within four percent of each udder on output per metre, which makes da design repeatable instead of lucky. From here on dere's a fleet — of two, eh." },
  "Flanking Run": { label: "Sneakin' Round Da Side", desc: "Supply gets to about eighteen a side, enough dat one guy can break off an' circle round wit'out leavin' da line empty-handed. Da season's first sneaky approach covers sixty feet in eleven seconds through a hundred-and-ten-degree arc, da runner carryin' five rounds an' gettin' to twelve feet before anybody looks. It works once, an' both sides post a lookout on da open side from den on." },
  "Sock Sling": { label: "Wool Sock Sling", desc: "A wool sock wit' a round in da toe, swung underhand an' let go at da bottom of da arc. Sixty feet at full stretch, dough effective range stays near thirty-five since only one throw in eight lands anywhere ya meant it to. Four guys get hit by dere own throw da first afternoon an' it stays in service anyhow, eh." },
  "Ambush": { label: "Ambush from Da Popples", desc: "Enough to crouch behind a popple wit' three in reserve an' fifteen in total supply. Position starts to matter, an' holdin' fire becomes a real option, dough two tries in three never get sprung 'cause somebody moves first, an' openin' range drops under fifteen feet. Engagements run three to five minutes, open after an average four-minute wait at a hit rate of one in two, an' come down to who's got more left when da first volley's done." },
  "Neighbourhood Loan": { label: "Lent to Da Neighbours", desc: "A machine leaves da property for da first time, lent to a house four doors down on da deal dat it comes back da same day. It does, three hours late, wit' grit in da trough an' a wing hinge sprung. Four more households ask for one within da week an' get told dere's only two in existence, ya know." },
  "Standoff": { label: "Standoff, Eh", desc: "Both sides got about twenty rounds an' neidder one's gonna spend 'em first. Da pause runs four to six minutes at forty feet apart, wit' about one pokin' throw a minute. It ends when a third guy shows up an' picks a side." },
  "Bucket Volley": { label: "Bucket Volley", desc: "A sand bucket gets swung to throw four rounds at once instead of one of 'em farther. Nuttin' goes past thirty feet an' nuttin's aimed, but da spread covers a twelve-foot front, which is da first time anybody goes after an area instead of a person, eh. Reload takes eleven seconds against a hand throw’s two." },
  "Two-Spreader Line": { label: "Two Spreaders in a Line", desc: "Both machines run in an overlappin' line, da second guy walkin' half a swath offset behind da first, which gets rid of da stripe seam a single pass leaves. Effective width goes to forty-eight centimetres of even cover all da way. Hollerin' da offset back an' forth flops right away, so da second operator just watches da first one’s left wheel instead, ya know." },
  "Duel": { label: "Da Duel", desc: "Two serious guys, about twenty rounds apiece, an' four to six watchin'. Rules get set ahead of time for range, where ya can hit, an' how many throws a side. First to five confirmed hits takes it, an' da whole ting runs eight to twelve minutes countin' resupply, eh." },
  "Coverage Contest": { label: "Coverage Contest", desc: "Da first competition: two operators, two machines, twenty minutes, most square feet of cover dat looks real. Da winner lays nineteen hundred square feet an' gets disqualified for a two-millimetre layer dat don't look like snow from da sidewalk. Da rule dat a layer's gotta be visible from da road at dusk goes in da record an' never comes out, ya know." },
  "Free-For-All": { label: "Free-For-All, Eh", desc: "Eight or nine guys, no teams, an' about twenty-five rounds each. Alliances last under thirty seconds an' average four per guy over da whole engagement. It runs fifteen minutes, nobody agrees who won, an' it ends when da last stockpile's spent." },
  "Spreader Rivalry": { label: "Spreader Rivalry", desc: "Da two sides of a fight dat's still goin' each get a machine, an' da war gets a second front, fought over da ground instead of wit' it. Neidder operator throws a ting all afternoon. Both come home havin' covered more ground dan dere whole side threw across, an' both get told dey missed da actual battle, eh." },
  "Snowball Fight": { label: "Snowball Fight, Eh", desc: "A real fight finally: six to ten guys, cover behind parked cars, an' a runnin' stockpile restocked mid-fight at about forty rounds a side. Effective range goes out to thirty-five feet. How long it lasts depends on how long yer hands stay warm, which means twenty to thirty minutes, ya know." },
  "Spreader Patent Dispute": { label: "Spreader Patent Spat", desc: "Two households both claim da machine's dere own design: eleven-centimetre screw, seven-centimetre pitch, slip clutch set to da kitchen-scale number. Da case gets heard in a garage by a panel of three older kids. Da original goes in as evidence: graph paper at four squares to da inch, one wheel drawn larger dan da other, dated in felt-tip in da corner. Da panel rules for da kid who drew it an' lets da other household print from da files, as long as every trough carries a scratched mark crediting da design." },
  "Counterfeit Spreaders": { label: "Knockoff Spreaders", desc: "Machines start showin' up dat never got printed from da files: wrong pitch, wrong flight depth, no clutch at all. Three of da four quit within a week, two by snappin' a screw shaft under load, exactly da way da clutch is dere to prevent. Da original design gets a scratched mark on da trough to tell it apart, an' da mark gets copied within nine days, eh." },
  "Running Battle": { label: "Runnin' Battle", desc: "Da fight quits holdin' still an' moves across three yards an' a driveway, coverin' four hundred feet over half an hour. Rounds get packed on da move at about one every fifteen seconds. Neidder side holds a spot more dan ninety seconds an' total supply never gets past fifty." },
  "Printed in a Basement": { label: "Printed Down in Da Basement", desc: "Production moves to a basement printer runnin' by itself overnight, eleven hours a machine, four machines a week if nuttin' warps. Da bottleneck quits bein' design an' turns into filament. Da guy runnin' da printer, who's never thrown a snowball in dis whole war, turns into da most important person on da block, ya know." },
  "Y-Frame Slingshot": { label: "Big Ol' Slingshot", desc: "Surgical tubing gets stretched between two popple saplings an' pulled back by a second guy layin' flat. Top range hits seventy-five feet, twice anyting thrown by hand, an' ya can't move it once it's built. It gets taken down after four days when da near sapling comes right outta da ground, eh." },
  "Extended Engagement": { label: "Goin' All Afternoon", desc: "Now da ammo outlasts da guys throwin' it, each side holdin' eighty or more at any time. Choppers soak through around da forty-minute mark, everybody quits fifteen to twenty minutes to dry out inside, an' den it starts right back up at full strength, ya know." },
  "Layer Doctrine": { label: "Layer Rules", desc: "A written standard shows up: five millimetres minimum, no seam ya can see, no spreadin' on ground a car uses. Da last of da three is da only one anybody enforces, an' it gets enforced, believe you me. Two operators get benched for a week over one pass across a driveway apron, an' neidder one argues." },
  "War of Attrition": { label: "War of Attrition", desc: "Neidder side can get run off an' neidder can resupply faster dan it throws. Production runs four rounds a minute a side against six goin' out. Fights now end when da material runs out after seventy to ninety minutes, wit' hit counts addin' up into da low hundreds, eh." },
  "Escorted Spreaders": { label: "Spreaders Wit' Bodyguards", desc: "A machine out in da open is a sittin' duck movin' at walkin' pace, an' both sides figure dat out da same afternoon. Operators get two throwers apiece whose only job is to keep da resurfacin' goin'. Cover rates drop by a third an' completion rates go from under half to nine in ten." },
  "Pitched Battle": { label: "Pitched Battle", desc: "Enough stuff for steady volleys from fixed spots at six to eight throws a minute a side, half of 'em slung off a full-size snow shovel at fifty-five feet against a hand throw’s thirty-five. Score gets kept, hits get hollered out, an' da runnin' count gets argued about about every third call. Fights go past an hour wit' eight to fourteen guys in 'em, eh." },
  "Rampart Skim Coat": { label: "Skim Coat on Da Walls", desc: "Spreaders get turned on da forts demselves, layin' a fresh two-millimetre coat over walls tromped grey by three days of use. It adds nuttin' structural. It makes da works look like new snow from forty feet, which is worth more dan da two millimetres, an' da habit sticks around for every later stretch of da war, ya know." },
  "Dug-In Line": { label: "Dug-In Line", desc: "Positions get scraped out instead of built up: a shallow trough eight inches deep, twenty inches wide an' twenty feet long, wit' da spoil banked in front to ten inches high an' fourteen across at da base. It stops a low throw an' nuttin' else, an' ya can't swing a sling from inside it. Two lines like dat face each udder at fifty feet an' neidder one gets left for da rest of da afternoon." },
  "Spreader Sabotage": { label: "Spreader Sabotage", desc: "Somebody puts gravel in an unattended buffer overnight. Da clutch does its job on da first push an' nuttin' on da machine gets hurt, but da trough's gotta be emptied by hand in da dark an' da mornin's resurfacin' don't happen. It's da first attack in da war aimed at equipment instead of people, an' it works better dan eidder, eh." },
  "First Wall": { label: "First Wall", desc: "Da first built ting of da season: knee-high at eighteen to twenty-four inches, packed by hand over about forty minutes. It runs eight to twelve feet long an' eight inches thick, enough to stop a straight throw from fifteen feet out, dough not a round lobbed over da top. One wall, one side, an' nuttin' facin' it yet, ya know." },
  "Backpack Spreader": { label: "Da Backpack Spreader", desc: "Standard personal issue shows up: a one-and-a-half-kilogram roller dat fills most of a school backpack an' lays a five-millimetre band twenty-eight inches wide at walkin' pace. It don't make snow; it moves it, gatherin' up da tromped-over leftovers of a fought-over yard into a workable ridge behind da fort line. One operator resurfaces sixty feet of stripped ground in da time a packer builds four rounds. Every wall crew puts in for one, eh." },
  "Wide-Body Spreader": { label: "Wide-Body Spreader", desc: "A bigger machine shows up wit' a fifty-centimetre trough an' wheels off a garden cart, layin' near double da swath at da same walkin' pace. It don't fit in any backpack an' takes two guys to lift into a wagon. Da trade's made right out in da open: portability spent for width, on a design whose whole original selling point was portability, ya know." },
  "Bat and Racquet": { label: "Bat an' Racquet", desc: "Rounds start gettin' hit instead of thrown, wit' a plastic bat an' a warped tennis racquet swiped from a garage, neidder one returned before spring. A clean hit carries sixty-five feet, near double a hand throw, but three rounds in five fall apart on da face of da swing. Packin' density gets bumped up just so dey survive da hit, eh." },
  "Wall and Ditch": { label: "Wall an' Ditch", desc: "Da stuff for da wall now comes outta a ditch two feet deep an' three wide, doublin' da effective height to four feet from da attackin' side an' takin' da wall to ten inches thick. Da whole works runs fourteen feet across an' takes ninety minutes. A straight charge has gotta cross da ditch, which adds about four seconds of hangin' out in da open." },
  "Fort Building": { label: "Buildin' Forts", desc: "Walls go up for real at thirty inches high, a foot thick an' sixteen feet of frontage, wit' two to three hundred rounds piled behind 'em. Teams of four to six form up a side, an' rules get hashed out for wall height, throw range, resupply intervals, an' which tools ya can swing. Buildin' runs ninety minutes before da first exchange, ya know." },
  "Fort-Side Spreader Bay": { label: "Spreader Bay in Da Fort", desc: "Forts start gettin' built wit' a covered bay in da back wall sized for a machine wit' its wings folded. Turnaround from a spent front to a resurfaced one drops under three minutes 'cause nobody walks back to a house. Every fort plan drawn after dis has da bay, includin' a bunch dat never get a machine, eh." },
  "Redoubt": { label: "Da Redoubt", desc: "A second, smaller position gets built behind da main wall as a fallback — six feet across, three feet high, fourteen inches thick, holdin' a reserve of eighty rounds. It gets used twice in an afternoon an' both times da line's back within ten minutes. Works per side now go past thirty feet of frontage." },
  "Spreader Crews": { label: "Spreader Crews", desc: "Runnin' one quits bein' a one-guy job: three to a machine — one pushin', one on da wings clearin' da intake, one haulin' reserve material. Steady output about triples over one operator. Da crew's da first ting in da war organised around a piece of equipment instead of around a fort or a buddy, ya know." },
  "Two Forts": { label: "Two Forts, Eh", desc: "Rival buildin' starts across da yard at forty to sixty feet apart. Both sides put up da front wall full height, three feet or better an' sixteen inches thick across eighteen feet of frontage, an' leave da flanks wide open across a sixty-degree approach. Combined labour runs four person-hours before eidder side throws a ting." },
  "Contested Yard": { label: "Fightin' Over Da Yard", desc: "Da forty feet of open ground between da forts changes hands six times in an afternoon. Neidder side holds it more dan eleven minutes, an' every try costs about forty rounds an' opens wit' a slingshot layin' twelve of 'em across da front. Combined stockpiles go past six hundred, an' production keeps up wit' spendin' for da first time all season, eh." },
  "Deniable Snowfall": { label: "Snow Dat Maybe Fell", desc: "An overnight run lays an even coat across four hundred feet of fought-over ground an' da other side wakes up sure it snowed. Da trick holds most of a mornin' an' falls apart on da tread marks, which ya can't miss an' which run in parallel lines. From den on both sides check for tread marks before believin' any weather at all, ya know." },
  "Fortified Position": { label: "Fortified Position", desc: "Walls eighteen inches thick an' forty inches high, enough to take a direct hit wit'out sheddin', runnin' twenty feet of frontage. One guy gets named ammo-maker an' works nonstop behind da line at a steady twelve rounds a minute, four of which go to da scoop crews as a standin' allocation. Standin' stockpiles go past five hundred a side, eh." },
  "Spreader Pickets": { label: "Spreader Pickets", desc: "Machines get posted at da edges of held ground to lay an' relay a fresh margin, so anybody crossin' it leaves a track. Dat turns da spreader from a supply engine into a lookout. A crossin' gets caught dis way at two in da afternoon an' da fight dat follows has eleven guys in it an' no snow dat wasn't laid down on purpose, ya know." },
  "Outworks": { label: "Outworks", desc: "Separate little positions get pushed twenty feet out front of da main wall to break up approaches — two a side, each five feet long, two feet high an' ten inches thick, manned by one guy. Dey fall on average within four minutes of a serious push an' get rebuilt overnight. Defended depth goes from six feet to about thirty, which puts da main wall outside a sling’s useful arc, eh." },
  "Glacis Blanketing": { label: "Blanketin' Da Glacis", desc: "Da open ground out front of da works gets resurfaced smooth an' even on purpose before a siege, so dere's no cover an' every footprint shows up plain. Three hundred and twenty feet of approach gets laid at five millimetres in about fifty minutes. Attackers come back by sneakin' up da one strip da wings couldn't reach, a two-foot margin along a fence, ya know." },
  "Siege Begins": { label: "Siege Starts", desc: "Neidder fort can get taken by a straight assault no more; three tries over two hours all come up short of da wall. Slings get turned upward to answer, lobbin' over da wall instead of at it from eighty feet, which is da first fire da defenders can't see comin'. Da standoff gets settled by stockpile size, not by any one charge. Both sides hold over eight hundred rounds an' make 'em faster dan dey can throw 'em, eh." },
  "Fortress & Siege": { label: "Fortress an' Siege", desc: "Da siege turns into just how tings are instead of an event. Each fort holds six wit' three in reserve, an' da ground between 'em goes unclaimed for stretches of forty minutes. Production an' spendin' even out near nine hundred rounds a side, an' neidder stockpile budges, ya know." },
  "Circumvallation": { label: "Wall All Da Way Around", desc: "A solid line gets built all da way around da other fort, a hundred and eighty feet of wall, three feet high an' a foot thick, closin' it in completely. It takes two days an' nine guys, an' da finished circuit gets walked by two slingers workin' opposite arcs. Resupply into da boxed-in position drops to zero an' da guys inside are down to four hundred rounds, eh." },
  "The Spreader Manual": { label: "Da Spreader Manual", desc: "Everyting learned gets written down in twenty-two hand-numbered pages: gate settings by material, da wing angle for a shallow verge, da nine-second clutch check, an' da standin' rule about drivin' lanes. It gets copied by hand four times an' every copy drifts. Three centuries later, four survivin' manuscripts disagree on da gate table an' all four cite da same lost original, ya know." },
  "Battlements": { label: "Battlements", desc: "Walls get taller at four to five feet an' twenty inches thick, four firin' notches a side at ten inches wide, cut to clear a sling when ya let go, an' a lookout spot. A tower sticks up two feet above da main wall, stretchin' sightlines to a hundred feet an' bumpin' warning on an approach from three seconds to twelve. Garrison gets to twelve per fort, eh." },
  "Night Spreading": { label: "Spreadin' After Dark", desc: "Resurfacin' moves to nighttime 'cause a machine at walkin' pace can't be defended in daylight. Da reflective strips on da wings an' grip, put on for road safety an' grumbled about, turn out to be da only way crews find each udder. Output per hour drops by a quarter; equipment losses drop to none, ya know." },
  "Watch Rotation": { label: "Standin' Watch", desc: "Positions get manned round da clock for da first time, in two-hour shifts across four guys per fort. Coverage runs first light to full dark, about nine hours, wit' a loaded sling kept at every notch da whole time. Two night tries get made in a week by parties of three, both spotted within forty feet of da wall against a hundred by daylight, an' both run off inside ninety seconds, eh." },
  "Spreader Depots": { label: "Spreader Depots", desc: "Machines quit belongin' to people an' start belongin' to positions, kept in numbered stores wit' spare wings, tread bands, an' clutch springs. Twelve machines an' forty spares across four depots. Time from a busted wing hinge to a workin' machine at da line drops from a day to eleven minutes." },
  "Multi-Fort Campaign": { label: "Whole Buncha Forts", desc: "Three or more strongholds hold da block across four hundred feet of frontage an' thirty guys. Alliances form up by stockpile size an' harden up soon as da first shared trench gets dug, lastin' an average of nine days apiece. No one fort can hold out against da other two togedder, ya know." },
  "Field Repair Kits": { label: "Field Fix-It Kits", desc: "A canvas roll wit' two clutch springs, a spare pinion, four tread bands, an' a jackknife goes out wit' every crew. Ninety percent of breakdowns get fixed right where dey happen now. Most-used ting in da kit is da knife, an' least-used is da pinion, which nobody's ever seen fail, eh." },
  "Fieldworks": { label: "Fieldworks", desc: "Buildin' moves past da forts into da ground between 'em: firin' steps, banked approaches, an' cut lanes totallin' three hundred feet of prepared position, two of 'em laid out for a bungee sling worked by two guys at eighty-five feet. Eleven people work it a full day. Every approach to every fort now crosses at least one built obstacle, ya know." },
  "Trench-Floor Spreading": { label: "Spreadin' Da Trench Floor", desc: "Skinny machines get built to fit a trench floor, twenty-two centimetres across da trough, layin' fresh footing over ground churned to mud an' ice by nonstop traffic. It don't help da fightin' one bit. It cuts da falls in half, an' a trench wit' fewer falls holds more hours of occupation, which is da whole argument for it, eh." },
  "Trenches": { label: "Trenches", desc: "Connected firin' spots get dug between da forts, two feet deep an' sixty to ninety feet total run. Movin' under cover becomes possible an' da fight goes below da snow line for da first time, at da cost of every flat-thrown gadget, none of which ya can swing from two feet down. Gettin' between positions goes from an exposed ten seconds to a covered thirty." },
  "Communication Trench": { label: "Supply Trench", desc: "A back trench just for dis links every forward spot to da ammo store, a hundred and twenty feet of it at three feet deep. Resupply runs dat used to draw fire now get done unseen in forty seconds. Da rate of fire ya can keep up at da front about doubles, ya know." },
  "Spreader Sappers": { label: "Spreader Sappers", desc: "Crews get hooked right onto da diggin' parties, layin' cover over da spoil so fresh earthworks quit announcin' demselves from way off. Forty feet of new trench gets hid in about eleven minutes. Both sides dig at night an' blanket it by dawn now, an' neidder one can tell how much of da other line is new, eh." },
  "Trench Warfare": { label: "Trench Warfare", desc: "Nobody stands up in da open no more, an' flat throwin' gives way to a lobbin' plank worked off da trench floor at sixty degrees. Da trench line runs two hundred feet across both positions an' every exchange comes from behind a lip of packed snow, droppin' hit rates from one in four to one in eleven. An afternoon of fightin' moves da front about six feet, ya know." },
  "Camouflage Layer": { label: "Camo Layer", desc: "Hidin' stuff becomes its own trade: matched depth, matched texture, an' some bumps put in by hand on purpose so it don't look machine-laid. A good crew can hide a battery emplacement in under twenty minutes. Da giveaway's always da edge, where laid snow meets fallen snow at a line too straight to be weather, eh." },
  "Tunnel Networks": { label: "Tunnels", desc: "Passages link up da trench system under da surface, three feet down an' a hundred and fifty feet all togedder. Da grown-ups get told once da network's done, an' da tunnels get looked over an' shored up wit' sled slats every six feet. Four entrances, two of 'em hid, ya know." },
  "Tunnel Spreaders": { label: "Tunnel Spreaders", desc: "Machines go underground, layin' dry floor cover through da tunnels where meltwater's made da goin' sketchy. Dey get pushed by feel, in da dark, wit' da wings folded an' da gate at four millimetres. Two crews run head-on into each udder in a tunnel neidder knew was connected, an' da map dat comes outta it is da most valuable paper made dat season, eh." },
  "Staff Sling": { label: "Staff Sling", desc: "A sling stuck on a three-foot staff an' swung two-handed from behind da wall, where dere's still room to stand up. Range gets to ninety-five feet against da sock sling’s seventy, an' da release arc clears da rampart wit'out showin' da thrower. Four get built an' two get ditched inside a week, 'cause dere's noplace safe to swing 'em, eh." },
  "Undermining": { label: "Diggin' Under", desc: "A tunnel gets driven under da other side's wall — twenty-two feet, four hours, two diggers workin' in shifts. Da cave-in takes out eight feet of frontage in a second and a half. Both sides start listenin' at da base of dere own walls every mornin', an' dat turns into standard practice, ya know." },
  "The Spreader Guild": { label: "Da Spreader Guild", desc: "Operators organise. To get in ya gotta show an even run at five millimetres, do a clutch check from memory, an' recite da surface rule word for word. Ninety-one members da first season, an' fourteen get turned down for spreadin' on a drivin' lane an' one for buildin' a machine wit'out a clutch, eh." },
  "The Keep": { label: "Da Keep", desc: "A central stronghold wit' a real inside room, seven feet long by six wide an' four feet at da ceiling, inside two-foot walls dat make da outside footprint eleven by ten. Dere's one per alliance instead of one per fort, both allied walls facin' out from it, an' it's cold, dark, drippin' about a drop a second, an' big enough for four guys sittin' down — kinda like camp in March. Inside temperature holds near twenty-eight degrees no matter what it reads outside." },
  "Keep Resurfacing": { label: "Touchin' Up Da Keep", desc: "Da inner works go on a maintenance rotation: every wall, every step, every parapet gets a fresh coat on a three-day cycle from a standin' crew of six. Da keep never looks used. Visitors from da outlyin' forts go home sayin' da garrison must not be fightin' at all, which is what dey're supposed to think, an' it's wrong, ya know." },
  "Inner Bailey": { label: "Inner Bailey", desc: "A second wall goes up behind both allied fronts, closin' in da shared keep an' da main store — sixty feet of circuit at five feet high an' thirty inches thick. Takin' eidder outer wall don't end nuttin' no more. Two full assaults reach an outer circuit in a week an' neidder gets through da inner, eh." },
  "Spreader Registry": { label: "Spreader Registry", desc: "Every machine in service gets numbered, logged, an' assigned to a position, wit' hours pushed an' material moved written down per unit. Four hundred and six are on da books an' eleven can't be found. Da registry outlasts da forts it was written to supply an' turns into, way later, da oldest continuous record eidder side's got, ya know." },
  "Ice-Armored Walls": { label: "Iced-Up Walls", desc: "Water gets poured over da ramparts on purpose, five to eight gallons a side, an' left overnight to glaze at about an eighth of an inch. Rounds now shatter when dey hit instead of packin' in — slung rounds worst of all, comin' in fast enough to bust on da glaze — cuttin' effective damage by about two thirds, an' both sides start glazin' within a day. Wall life triples, eh." },
  "Armoured Spreaders": { label: "Armoured Spreaders", desc: "Machines workin' under fire get a curved shield over da trough an' a glazed ice apron on da pushin' side, addin' four kilograms to a design built to weigh one and a half. Crew losses durin' resurfacin' drop by two thirds. Output per hour drops by a fifth, an' every crew offered da shield takes it, ya know." },
  "Glazing Crews": { label: "Glazin' Crews", desc: "Glazin' becomes a standin' job: three guys per fort, forty gallons a night, hauled from a basement tap in relays over sixty feet, eleven trips a night. Coverage goes from da front face to da whole circuit, about two hundred square feet at a third of an inch a night. Sections dat don't get done get marked on da map an' become da standard target, eh." },
  "Spreader Doctrine": { label: "Spreader Doctrine", desc: "Redistribution gets a doctrine instead of a manual: resurface before da packers run dry, never resurface while somebody's watchin', never resurface da same ground twice in a day. It gets argued about for a generation an' taken up near unchanged. Da third rule's dere 'cause ground laid twice looks laid, an' ground dat looks laid is a target, ya know." },
  "Sling Corps": { label: "Sling Corps", desc: "Slingers quit workin' alone an' get grouped into two ranks of fifteen, throwin' on a called count. A massed release puts thirty rounds into a twenty-foot square inside two seconds, which no one guy's aim ever managed. Trainin' up to a usable standard takes nine sessions an' about a third never get dere, eh." },
  "Spreader Corps": { label: "Spreader Corps", desc: "Redistribution turns into a trade wit' its own crews: nine operators in a rollin' line, wings out, feedin' nonstop off da plough berm at da yard’s edge. Dey lay a solid forty-foot front of fresh cover per pass an' turn a bare, fought-over lawn back into a supplied position in under four minutes. Packers now draw from ground da spreaders resurfaced instead of from da sky, an' Heikki Lunta quits bein' da only supplier, ya know." },
  "Siege Engines": { label: "Siege Engines", desc: "Da first catapult, put togedder from a sled, a fence post, an' four bungee cords taken wit'out askin' an' missed within a day. It launches a four-inch round a measured hundred and ten feet, about triple hand-throw range, den falls apart on da second try. Puttin' it togedder took two hours an' five guys, eh." },
  "Spreader Liaison": { label: "Spreader Go-Between", desc: "A runner gets stuck between da spreader crews an' da engine batteries so resurfacin' an' bombardment quit happenin' in da same square at da same time. Before da go-between, four machines get lost to friendly fire in a month. After, none, an' da runner's da only guy in da sector allowed to stop a battery mid-load, ya know." },
  "Ballista": { label: "Ballista", desc: "A flat-shootin' engine built on a bicycle inner tube an' two fence uprights, aimed instead of lobbed. It puts one round through a firin' notch at a hundred and thirty feet, wit' one shot in four landin' inside a two-foot circle. Reload takes fifty seconds, an' dat's its whole problem, eh." },
  "Counter-Battery": { label: "Counter-Battery", desc: "Engines now get built just to wreck udder engines, at ranges out to a hundred and forty feet. Four are in service across da block an' three get knocked out within a week, two of 'em by udder engines. Median workin' life of a siege engine drops to nine shots, ya know." },
  "Spread-and-Pack Cycle": { label: "Spread-an'-Pack Cycle", desc: "Da two trades get hooked togedder official: a spreader lays a fresh bed, packers work it within da hour while it's still bindin', an' da stripped ground goes back in da rotation. Round quality goes up measurably, 'cause snow packed within an hour of bein' laid holds better dan snow packed off tromped ground. Output per guy per day about doubles an' never drops again, eh." },
  "Trebuchet": { label: "Trebuchet", desc: "A counterweight engine wit' a pivotin' arm an' a bucket of packed snow for mass, throwin' two hundred and sixty feet against da hundred and forty of anyting else in service. Buildin' it takes nine hours an' a pit dug to seat da frame. It outranges every counter-battery engine on da block, which ends da counter-battery advantage in a day, ya know." },
  "Ammunition Factory": { label: "Ammo Factory", desc: "A real production line wit' a foreman an' six workers. Output runs sixty to ninety rounds an hour, standin' inventory goes past two thousand, an' every round gets checked for a three-inch diameter, even density, an' a fit in da engine cups before it gets stacked. Rejects settle around one in eight, eh." },
  "Resurfacing Line": { label: "Resurfacin' Line", desc: "Da ammo factory gets a matchin' spreader line runnin' da opposite way: one crew packs snow into rounds, da udder lays snow back on stripped ground so da packers never run dry. Throughput settles near three hundred metres of resurfaced front an hour against nineteen hundred rounds packed. Da two lines get timed against each udder on a board by da door, an' for da first week da spreaders are winnin', ya know." },
  "Engine Shops": { label: "Engine Shops", desc: "Engines quit gettin' built where dey're used: two shops get set up behind da line wit' frames, arms, an' cut tubing. Build time drops from nine hours to three, an' a wrecked engine gets rebuilt instead of written off. Standin' spares run to four complete frames an' sixty feet of tubing, eh." },
  "Spreader Foundry": { label: "Spreader Foundry", desc: "A works gets set up to mould screws an' troughs instead of printin' 'em, in a copolymer picked 'cause homopolymer shatters in da cold, an' da cold's da whole operating condition, ya know. Output goes from four machines a week to sixty. Da material call gets made once, by a guy who tests two samples in a freezer, an' nobody ever looks at it again." },
  "Quarry Works": { label: "Snow Quarries", desc: "Clean snow turns into da limit instead of labour, an' cuttin' sites get opened up away from da fightin' — four of 'em, each good for about six hundred rounds a day, a fifth of it cut dense enough for da engines. Haul distance averages three hundred feet. Two of da four get fought over within da first week an' change hands three times between 'em, eh." },
  "Ranging Stakes": { label: "Rangin' Stakes", desc: "Fire quits bein' guesswork: stakes get pounded in every twenty-five feet out to two hundred feet, an' every engine gets walked onto its target wit' three rangin' shots. Hit rate at max range goes from one in eleven to one in four. A rangin' book gets kept per engine an' copied whenever crews rotate, ya know." },
  "Screw Standardization": { label: "Same Screw for Everybody", desc: "Every screw in service gets brought to one pattern — eleven centimetres over, three and a half core, seven pitch — so any screw fits any trough anywhere on da front. Nine hundred off-pattern machines get called back an' re-cored. Da pitch dey pick is da one argued over on paper at two ten-thousandths of an inch of snow, unchanged, an' nobody alive now knows who argued for it, eh." },
  "Front Lines": { label: "Front Lines", desc: "Da war's outgrown one block an' runs across four, about two thousand feet of fought-over frontage. Da main wall gets bumped to six feet high, three feet thick, an' two hundred and twenty feet long, an' now dere's just one per two-fort alliance, both allied forts hunkered behind one shared face; three alliances put six hundred and sixty feet of da frontage behind wall. Territory gets mapped on notebook paper, held by one guy a side, an' fixed up after every change of position — about nine times a day. Combined head count goes past sixty an' engine density settles at one per four hundred feet of frontage, ya know." },
  "Spreader Reconnaissance": { label: "Spreader Scoutin'", desc: "Crews get sent forward just to lay ground an' come back tellin' what dey saw, which is more dan any scout gets, 'cause a spreader's got a reason to be walkin' slow across open ground. Four sectors get mapped dis way in a week. Both sides figure out what's goin' on about da same time an' start readin' each udder’s laid ground as intelligence, eh." },
  "Salients": { label: "Salients", desc: "Da line quits bein' straight. Three bulges push into da udder side's territory sixty to a hundred feet deep, each defended on three sides across a hundred and eighty feet of wall an' each needin' about forty percent more guys per foot of frontage. Each one's held by two engines firin' on divergent arcs, an' two of da three get given up on purpose within a week, ya know." },
  "Counter-Spreader Fire": { label: "Shootin' at Da Spreaders", desc: "Batteries start rangin' on resurfacin' crews as dere own kind of target, on da idea dat a front ya can't resupply ya can't hold. It's da first time in da war da equipment's worth more dan da position. Spreader losses da first month run to thirty-one machines, an' every one gets replaced from da foundry inside a week, eh." },
  "Bombardment": { label: "Bombardment", desc: "Indirect fire goes nonstop instead of now an' den, at a steady forty rounds an hour per engine across nine engines. Nuttin's aimed at a person; da target's da wall itself, an' glazed frontage dat once lasted a week now lasts two days. Both sides start fixin' under fire as a standin' job, ya know." },
  "Supply Lines": { label: "Supply Lines", desc: "Ammo's gotta get moved to where it's needed over hauls of five hundred feet or more. Sleds get requisitioned, two a side, from four households dat don't get asked, one of 'em saved for counterweight stock, routes get fixed, an' delivery rate — about four hundred rounds an hour — sets da pace of da whole war. Forward positions hold ninety minutes of supply, eh." },
  "Spreader Convoys": { label: "Spreader Convoys", desc: "Resupply goes mobile. Spreaders get wheeled forward on da supply lines demselves, loaded from back depots an' run up to resurface positions under fire. A convoy of six covers two miles of tromped approach in four hours. Each machine hauls its own four-litre reserve for da stretches where dere's no snow alongside da track, an' doctrine reclassifies da spreader as a supply engine instead of a weapon, ya know." },
  "Spreader Rail Head": { label: "Spreader Rail Head", desc: "A sled tramway gets run up to within four hundred feet of da line, haulin' machines an' dere reserve material forward wit'out a push. Sixty machines a day show up at da head. It gets wrecked twice, rebuilt twice, an' da second rebuild moves it two hundred feet farther back, which nobody gripes about, eh." }
});
